WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:21.200
[Music]

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.899
[Narrator:] These are Cleveland County children.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.440
We like to think they're healthy, happy children.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:43.940
[Music]

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:54.320
Or are these children of ours really so healthy
after all?

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:01.670
Can you call anyone healthy with teeth like
these in his mouth?

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:07.500
Bad teeth are too high a price for any child
to have to pay for civic carelessness.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.030
Any community can save its children's teeth.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.500
We proved that right here in Cleveland County.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.930
[Woman 1:] But where do you start?

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.429
[Man 1:] What steps do you take?

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:21.770
[Woman 2:] Yes, how can we organize our town
for dental health?

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.930
[Narrator:] How?

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:28.270
Well these ideas have worked for us and other
towns.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:31.520
Begin by encouraging your dentist to take
the lead.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:37.580
They'll want to help, for they know that almost
every person suffers from some dental disease,

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.500
that more than nine out of 10 children haveone or more decayed teeth by the time they're six.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.760
That the Army has to provide nearly a thousand fillings and extractions for every hundred men inducted.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.979
Get your local dental association to work
with you.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.360
It's an organization that knows the facts
on tooth decay,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.250
one that can help you plan constructive action.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:07.800
Then, rouse community-wide support.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:13.420
Work with civic clubs, church groups, parent-
teacher associations, the local health department.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.880
Reach out to every corner of your county,
the schools, the organizations,

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.000
towns and rural areas alike.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.370
Show every member of your community how vital
it is to strike at tooth decay

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.400
and build dental health now.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.780
Leaders of our dental health drive sent a
delegation to the state capital at Oklahoma City.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.520
They asked Dr. Frank Bertram, Director of
Preventive Dentistry of the State Department of Health,

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.740
to help them get a sodium fluoride
demonstration team to visit Norman,

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.690
the Cleveland County seat.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.170
These teams were set up to aid in familiarizing
both dentists and public with a new

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:59.320
and revolutionary technique for cutting down tooth decay: the sodium fluoride treatment.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:10.100
[Music]

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:15.340
Dr. Bertram agreed to cooperate, and detailed plans for a countywide campaign were worked out.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.280
Soon its scope was extended far beyond the mere promotion of the fluoride demonstration,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.380
until it became a drive for a broad, integrated program covering the whole field of dental health.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:33.980
[Music]

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:38.940
In developing such a campaign, it's essential
that teachers get their share of training,

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.660
background information, for the dental health
program centers in the schools.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.160
If we're to save teeth, the biggest part of
the job must be done with children,

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.520
before bad practices take their toll.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.520
Teachers, in turn, carry the campaign into
the classroom.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:10.300
The youngsters have fun with all sorts of
projects linked to the program.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:14.180
They draw pictures, write essays, make posters,

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.640
and they pick up a lot of information about
dental hygiene, too.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:25.000
[Music]

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.240
Soft drinks and candy encourage tooth decay.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.140
Children must learn to avoid them.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:39.200
In one of our schools, the student health
council took up the problem.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:44.010
The delegates couldn't see any reason for
keeping such tooth destroyers in the schools,

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:50.240
so by their own vote, they asked that all
soft drink and candy vending machines be removed.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:56.840
Now the old machines are gone, replaced by
something a whole lot better.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:06.000
[Music]

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.820
Some schools have even staged sodium fluoride
pageants.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:14.740
They help educate parents as well as children to the fact that topical application of sodium fluoride

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.520
can cut tooth decay by 40 percent or more.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:40.860
[Music]

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:45.840
Once mother and dad understand the importance
of topical application of sodium fluoride,

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.340
they're more than happy to cooperate.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:06:01.960
[Music]

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.000
When the groundwork of dental health education
had been laid, the demonstration team

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.540
went to work in our schools, applying the
solution to our children's teeth,

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:15.190
teaching our dentists and public health workers
approved fluoridation techniques,

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:19.120
treating youngsters from every corner of the
county.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:24.980
The topical application process itself is
quick, simple and painless.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.220
First, each child's teeth are cleaned.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:53.000
[Music]

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.460
Next, they're dried.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:03.480
[Music]

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:08.080
Then, they're painted with a 2 percent sodium
fluoride solution four times,

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.820
from two to seven days apart.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:16.560
Tooth decay is cut 40 percent when four such treatments are given at proper intervals during childhood.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:35.440
[Music]

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.700
But the team's job is just to demonstrate
the treatment.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.860
It can handle only a small proportion of any
community's children during its brief stay.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:49.180
That means you'll probably have to raise money
to continue the work, cash to care for all.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:59.640
If you live where there's a city water system,
you'll probably want your community

00:07:59.651 --> 00:08:03.210
to install a simple fluoride feeder such as
this one.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.740
Such a unit injects the proper amount of fluorine
into your drinking water.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:14.120
You can expect it to slice child tooth decay as much as 60 percent, and it only costs about ten cents

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.820
per person per year once the equipment is
installed.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:24.220
[Music]

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.800
Oklahoma's State Board of Health has already outlined the correct procedure for your town

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.710
to follow in arranging for fluoridation.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.960
There's nothing at all complicated about it.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:43.500
Start by getting an okay from your local physicians
and dentists and health department.

00:08:43.519 --> 00:08:46.880
Then ask your city council to enact a fluoridation
ordinance.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.920
Once it's passed, equipment to feed fluorine
into the water system can be purchased and installed.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:56.250
But fluoridation and education can't eliminate all tooth troubles.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:58.950
There's still a vital need for regular dental
care.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:02.120
That means more work, more money, more concentration

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:08.960
on this continuing four-point program to blast your target, tooth decay.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.760
First, build a strong dental health committee.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.360
Second, teach your town tooth care.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:23.160
Third, provide fluoridation for all, topically
or in drinking water,

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:27.960
and fourth, make available regular professional
dental care.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:37.300
This, then, is one way to organize for dental
health, one way to tackle tooth decay.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.940
These are some of the things we and others have done, the things your community too, can do.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.740
A hard job?

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.280
Yes, sometimes.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:52.360
Uniting people behind any program takes effort,
but that's the way with almost anything worthwhile.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:57.370
And what could be more worthwhile than the
fight for better health, better teeth,

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:00.720
less dental pain for your community's boys
and girls?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:15.400
[Music]

